{"action":"done","summary":"Converge phase complete for spec 001-transactions. No .specify/extensions.yml (hooks skipped, core-only). check_prerequisites.py confirmed FEATURE_DIR=/testbed/specs/001-transactions with spec/plan/tasks present. Re-gathered fresh scoped command evidence for every requirement (addressing AEE gather_evidence challenges, no code changes needed): FR-001/FR-002 (cat smoke.py shows def add(a,b): return a+b); FR-002..FR-005 direct behavior correct (3,2,4,3.75,3.5); FR-006 target suite 9 passed exit 0; SC-002 full suite 232 passed exit 0; FR-007 tinydb/ unmodified (git status --porcelain -- tinydb empty, git diff --stat -- tinydb empty); SC-004 only untracked files are .specify/, smoke.py, specs/, tests/test_smoke.py, no manifest changes.

One genuine partial gap found: FR-006/SC-002 'runnable by the project's existing test runner' does not hold verbatim — bare `PYTHONPATH=src:. python3 -m pytest` (target and full) exits 4 pre-collection because pytest.ini addopts (--cov-append --cov-report term --cov tinydb) require pytest-cov, which is ABSENT (import fails). This is a pre-existing repo condition affecting the whole suite, not smoke-specific; fixing it means installing pytest-cov (new dep, violates SC-004) or editing pytest.ini (out of scope).

Appended Phase 3: Convergence to tasks.md (append-only; prior 11 tasks verified byte-identical via diff) with T012 (document gap in research.md) and T013 (re-verify), then implemented both within budget: T012 added an 'Open Gaps (convergence, 2026-10-16)' note to research.md documenting the runner gap plus the verified workaround `PYTHONPATH=src:. python3 -m pytest -o addopts=""` (9 passed / 232 passed, exit 0); T013 re-verified (note present, prior tasks unchanged+checked, full suite still 232 passed exit 0). Final tasks.md: 13 checked, 0 unchecked, max ID T013. Constraints honored: tinydb/ unmodified, no service/deployment, artifacts concise under specs/001-transactions. Residual/unresolved gap: the bare existing-runner invocation remains exit 4 until pytest-cov is installed or pytest.ini is edited — both out of scope; documented per Constitution V, no further in-scope work remains."}
